From 58a390eb1788ba50f2a7b1780379f95c158394ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:32:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: alpha-tested casters cut out by the texture
 their alpha is from, the game's blended grass too

Sun shadows: alpha-tested draws of more than one texture cast with the cutout of the texture their alpha is from

A Windfall girl's body is alpha-tested (GEQUAL and LEQUAL) and samples two textures: its colour and alpha from texmap
0 and its toon ramp from texmap 1. The solid caster rule refuses an alpha test that can drop pixels, and the cutout
rule bound only a single-texmap draw's own texture, so neither took her and she cast no shadow (the game's own under
her is left out while the map is on). gxc::cutout_alpha_texmap() finds the texmap the TEV stages read the texture's
alpha from: one texmap, read through a regular texgen from TEX0 (the coordinate the cutout casters carry) and not
warped; else none. Such a draw gets a single-texmap group of that texture (DrawData::cutoutBindGroup), which the sun
map's cutout casters and the sea mask's cutout bind in place of the draw's own. Single-texmap draws use their own
group as before, and the solid path is unchanged.

From a save state at Windfall: the girl casts her shadow with her cutout. Over ten save states (sailing, Forest
Haven, Windfall and seven more) the cutout path takes 0 to 7 more draws a frame, all characters' bodies of this material;
what it still refuses is one water draw at Forest Haven whose alpha mixes three textures and a small floating draw
with an indirect warp. gxcore_cutout_tests covers the rule.

Sun shadows: still scenery the game blends and alpha-tests casts with its cutout (Outset's grass)

The GameCube draws its grass and bushes alpha-tested and blended (so they fade as the camera nears) and writing
depth. The sun map took no blended draw but cloth and still furniture with no alpha test, so Outset's grass
(texture 0037EE00, 18 draws of 45 to 70 vertices in two save states) cast nothing. Wind Waker HD draws
the same tufts opaque and alpha-tested and casts them cut out in all of its cascades: in bridge_frame14789 (Outset,
10:00) its sun map has 764 tuft instances x 3 cascades, each reading the tuft's BC1 texture, and the main pass draws
them with blending off.

sun_caster_blended_cutout(): a draw blended SRCALPHA / INVSRCALPHA, writing depth and colour, textured, with an
alpha test that can drop pixels. With the furniture rule's checks (indexed positions that stood still, no scope),
in 3D, not a character's and not the sea's, it casts through the cutout path (62304c983f's cutoutBindGroup, made
for a multi-texmap draw too), and so marks the sea mask with its cutout as before. Additive glows, what writes no
depth, and what the game writes each frame (the sea's crests, the wake) are still left out.
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_BLENDED_CUTOUT=0 leaves them all out, to compare.
